---
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Faq from "../components/Faq.astro";
---

<Layout title="FAQs">
  <div class="container">
    <PageHeader title="Frequently Asked Questions" />
    <Faq question="Where is it?">
      <p>
        FarmCamp is located at <a
          href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/ugQjvmcDP8rrVvndA"
          target="_blank">826 Co Rd 27, Tuskegee, AL 36083</a
        >. More information on the property can be found at <a
          href="https://gofarmcamp.com"
          target="_blank">gofarmcamp.com</a
        >. Reservations for Passage must be made through the Shotgun ticketing
        platform.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reservations made through the FarmCamp website for the dates of Passage
        will not be honored.
      </p>
    </Faq>
    <Faq
      question="I heard that it’s pretty remote, so what about the facilities?"
    >
      <p>
        At our previous property, there were very few creature comforts and
        attendees were expected to provide virtually everything themselves. At
        Farmcamp, you will still be camping, but it's more of a camping resort
        than a raw property. Features include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          A beautifully designed bath house with both private and shared
          showers, air conditioning, and lockers
        </li>
        <li>A full service bar</li>
        <li>Integrated filtered water system</li>
        <li>
          RV sites and primitive camping with access to power hookups and water
        </li>
        <li>Glamping tents and Cabins for rent</li>
        <li>Plenty of space for car camping and tent-only camping</li>
        <li>Pool and In-ground hot tub</li>
      </ul>
    </Faq>
    <Faq question="Is Passage a Burn?">
      <p>
        In short, No. Passage has always abided the 11 principles, burned an
        effigy, and bore the Punk Rock ethos of its founders, but lacked some
        essential burn mechanics, like theme camps.  This year, we are
        consciously making a decision to leave the semblance of being a boutique
        burn behind, leaning into the full-scale curation of the event and
        embracing a cash bar, merch sales, etc. We are burners at heart and will
        always participate in regional burns when feasible for us, but Passage
        is in a category all its own. That said, the Principles are still at the
        core of this event. Radical Inclusion, Immediacy, Radical Self-reliance,
        Civic Responsibility, Communal effort, LNT, Immediacy, Radical Self
        Expression, Consent as Sacred Responsibility. Read the principles, use
        your head and your heart, take care of one another.
      </p>
    </Faq>
    <Faq question="What should I bring?">
      <p>
        In short, everything you'll need to survive and thrive in the woods for
        a weekend. It will be hot during the day and short sleeve cool at night.
      </p>
    </Faq>
    <Faq question="Will there be food vendors?">
      <p>
        We are still working on the answer to this question. We may have a
        couple of food trucks, but you should plan to bring meals and a way to
        prepare them.
      </p>
    </Faq>
    <Faq question="What’s the alcohol situation?">
      <p>
        There will be a full service bar open for service a good portion of the
        weekend, You’re ALSO welcome to bring whatever alcoholic beverages you’d
        like and share at your pleasure! Please no glass bottles at all,
        anywhere, and no littering, please and thank you.
      </p>
    </Faq>
    <Faq question="Wait, what about water?">
      <p>
        You should bring what you think you'll need, however, there will be
        refill coolers scattered around the area where you can fill your water
        bottle or have a quick drink. The main pavilion (Showers, Bar, Pool) has
        a filtered water system, so the tap water is perfectly safe to drink!
      </p>
    </Faq>
    <Faq question="Will there be cell service on the property?">
      <p>Cell service is fine.</p>
    </Faq>
    <Faq question="What if it rains?">
      <p>
        We will certainly get wet! Bring rain gear, umbrellas, and pop-up
        canopies to get out of the rain if you’re particularly sensitive to it.
        There are also some common areas to huddle out of the rain, in several
        different locations. The party will go on, barring a severe
        thunderstorm. If lightning gets intense, we recommend you sit in your
        car to wait it out. That’s worst case scenario. Unfortunately, this
        comes with the territory of underground camping festivals.
      </p>
      <p>Submit to the moment and let’s make some memories.</p>
    </Faq>
    <Faq
      question="I need to arrive after the posted 9pm gate closing, can I still get in?"
    >
      <p>
        Yes! We <strong>strongly</strong> recommend you get there before dark so
        you can get the lay of the land before liftoff. But we know that’s not
        possible for everyone. If you get there after dark, just follow the
        signs and instructions provided to you at the gate. Piece of cake.
      </p>
    </Faq>
    <Faq question="Can I bring my kids?">
      <p>Passage is a 21+ event, no exceptions.</p>
    </Faq>
    <Faq question="Can I bring my dog?">
      <p>
        Nope. While we love the furry friends as much as anyone, pets are not
        allowed at Passage for a robust list of reasons. If your dog is a
        service animal, however, it is welcome to accompany you in that
        capacity.
      </p>
    </Faq>
    <Faq question="Can I bring my flow/fire toys?">
      <p>
        Hell yes! If you intend to spin fire, please touch base with us so we
        can put you in touch with our fire performance leads who will have final
        say on permission, protocol, and fire circle mechanics.
      </p>
    </Faq>
    <Faq question="Can I invite my friends?">
      <p>
        Yes! If you’ve been invited to this event, we trust you to invite people
        who you believe are well suited.
      </p>
    </Faq>
    <Faq question="Can I bring my RV?">
      <p>
        Yes! you wIll need to purchase an RV pass alongside your Admission
        Ticket.
      </p>
    </Faq>

    <style lang="scss">
      .container {
        max-width: 800px;
      }
    </style>
  </div>
</Layout>
